# Load-bearing rules for shared:create-skill.
# This skill teaches the house pattern, so an error here propagates into every
# skill scaffolded afterwards — that is exactly how `allowed-tools` reached
# both shipped agents. The frontmatter table and verbosity guidance are lookup
# material and live in references/; the rules that must not drift are here.

the house pattern is Steps then Output format then Constraints :: Steps.*Output format.*Constraints|## Steps
name must match the skill's directory :: name.*match|matches the directory|match.*directory
description must be quoted :: quoted
user-invocable is explicit :: user-invocable
argument-hint is required when the skill reads $ARGUMENTS :: argument-hint
$ARGUMENTS is the only valid substitution, never positional :: ARGUMENTS
positional $0/$1 are rejected :: \$0|positional
agents take comma-separated tools:, not allowed-tools :: comma-separated|tools:
allowed-tools is silently ignored in agent frontmatter :: silently ignored|ignored
